  era: "Section 36 \xB7 Indian Economy Through History \xB7 Across the ages"
  title: Maritime trade
  text: Indian Ocean trade linked India with Arabia, East Africa, South-East Asia and China, with the monsoon winds setting the sailing seasons. Gujarati, Tamil and Arab merchants were especially active on these routes.
